{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Network in Computer Based Information Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about networks in Computer Based Information Systems."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about relational database management system in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level.  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verb + Ing and to + Verb in Affirmative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Gerund</b> and <b>infinitive</b> are forms of the verb that act as nouns. The <b>gerund</b> is formed with the \u201c<b>\u2013ing</b>\u201d and the <b>infinitive</b> with the preposition \u201c<b>to</b>\u201d"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've finished writing my report for my boss about the telecommunication networks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some verbs can be followed by an infinitive or a gerund without causing a change in meaning; however, some other verbs only accept one of the two forms. In this case, you have to learn these verbs as there are no rules to make a distinction. Check the following chart to learn about some verbs that take the <b>infitinitive</b> and <b>gerund</b> form."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Infinitive</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Gerund</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Afford\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Consider \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Agree\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Delay \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Intend \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Involve \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Need \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Suggest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plan \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Risk\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You started saying that telecommunication methods consist of computers, communications processors, and other devices interconnected by communications media and controlled by communications software."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Networks"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A network consists of two or more computers that are linked to each other so they can share resources (such as printers and CDs), exchange files, or allow electronic communications. The computers on a network may be linked through cables, telephone lines, radio waves, satellites, or infrared light beams."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Discuss the network resources, first the communications media: such as twisted pair wire, coaxial cable, fiber-optic cable, and microwave systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are different types of networks in information systems. The Internet, intranets, and extranets have become essential to the proper operations of all types of organizations and their computer-based information systems. </br></br>Network resources include:  \t"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Communications media:</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Such as twisted pair wire, coaxial cable, fiber-optic cable, microwave systems, and communication satellite systems.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Network support:</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This  category includes all of the people, hardware, software, and data resources that directly support the operation and use of a communications network. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Two very common types of networks include:</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Local Area Network (LAN)</br></br> Wide Area Network (WAN)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Other networks :</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Metropolitan Area Networks (MAN), a Wireless LAN (WLAN), or a Wireless WAN (WWAN).\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mention the generic category; that is Network support including people, hardware, software, and data resources that support the operation and use of a communications network."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "trainee"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " a person who is learning and practicing the skills of a particular job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'm the new IT trainee and I've finished writing my report for my boss."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hassle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "problem, difficulty or trouble"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want you to review it; If it isn't a hassle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "merge"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to combine or join together"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Computer systems merge computers and communications."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "intranet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an internal  system of connected computers that allows people within an organization to communicate with each other and share information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Consider including that telecommunication is a collection of nodes together with Internet, intranets, and extranets."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "extranet"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a system of computers that makes it possible for organizations to communicate with each other and share information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Consider including that telecommunication is a collection of nodes together with Internet, intranets, and extranets."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wire "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a piece of thin metal thread with a layer of plastic around it, used for carrying electric current:"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: First, the communications media, such as twisted-pair wire."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le01ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for more information about telecommunication networks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a poster where you point out the benefits of telecommunication networks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare a 5 minute presentation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with the calss. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I identify network resources."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the benefits of telecommunication networks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the benefits of telecommunication networks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with the class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Karen</strong>: I'm the new IT trainee, and I've finished writing my report for my boss about the telecommunication networks at this company. However, I want you to review it; If it isn't a hassle! </br><strong>Lenny</strong>: Sure, let me see. You started saying that telecommunication methods consist of computers, communications processors, and other devices interconnected by communications media and controlled by communications software. I suggest starting with a definition and then adding these lines. Furthermore, consider including that telecommunication is a collection of nodes that along with the Internet, Intranet, and Extranet aim to increase the success of the operations in any company. </br></div>"}, {"time": "51000", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Karen</strong>: I included some information about the importance of a network in information systems too. Understanding the concept of network resources is essential; this is why I mentioned that the success of every enterprise depends on how well it manages its networks. Also, cost is reduced by sharing hardware and software resources; therefore, computer systems merge computers and communications. </br></div>"}, {"time": "82000", "image": "enpe7n7le01ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>Lenny</strong>: When you're in the IT field, it's important to understand the role of the network for the system, so you can also mention that computer networks allow the user to access remote programs and remote databases. They can belong to the same organization or they can be used to access other enterprises or public sources providing communication possibilities in a faster way. Computer networks may increase the organizational learning rate and the number of possibilities to connect devices, as well as reduce costs as you mentioned it. Also, discuss the network resources; first, the communications media, such as twisted-pair wire, coaxial cable, fiber-optic cable, microwave systems, and communication satellite systems.  Second, mention the generic category. That is network support including people, hardware, software, and data resources that support the operation and the use of a communications network. </br><strong>Karen</strong>: Thanks, Lenny. I knew you'd be of great help.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le01ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le01ob05re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what telecommunication networks consist of."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can present information about the importance of a network in information systems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say what network resources include."}, {"type": "Free H